		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The polling option set is fixed. Fixture App polls ISO 14443 and ISO 15693 together because the chip families it recognises are split across the two, and picking one at call time would make a mistyped intent look like a dead tag. The "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "internal",
					"slug": "reference/chip-support",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "chip support matrix"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " lists which part number answers on which protocol, and the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "internal",
					"slug": "developer/architecture",
					"anchor": "module-graph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "module graph"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " shows where "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSession"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " sits."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "alertMessage"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " can be rewritten while the session is live. The sheet re-renders in place and the radio link survives, which is how the write path swaps \"Hold your iPhone near the tag\" for \"Writing, keep holding\"."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The store listing calls this \"tap and go\", and the phrase sets a budget the API has to meet: 700 ms from "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "begin(_:)"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " to a written tag on a NTAG215 at 137 bytes. Anything slower and a user lifts the phone early."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "the-state-machine",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The state machine"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "There are four states: "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".idle"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".polling"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".connected"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".finished"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". On a successful connect the state is "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".polling"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " \u2192 "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".connected"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", and every callback from that point runs on the session queue rather than on the main queue. Publishing to SwiftUI therefore needs an explicit hop; "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSessionStore"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " does that hop once so view code never has to."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A session that ends for any reason, including the user cancelling the sheet, lands in "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": ".finished"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and cannot be restarted. Create a new "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSession"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " per operation. Holding one and calling "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "begin(_:)"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " twice throws "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSessionError.sessionSpent"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "delegate-callbacks",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Delegate callbacks"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "TagSessionDelegate"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " has three methods and none of them is optional."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"style": "bullet",
			"tight": true,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "session(_:didConnect:)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " gives you the detected tag and the chip identity the app resolved from its UID and capability container."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "session(_:didFinish:)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " reports a completed read or write, with the byte count and the elapsed time."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "session(_:didFail:)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " reports a "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "TagSessionError"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": ". It is the only place the app surfaces error copy, so the strings live beside the cases rather than in the view layer."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Do not call UIKit or SwiftUI from any of the three without dispatching to the main queue first."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "errors",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Errors"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "table",
			"align": [
				null,
				null,
				null
			],
			"header": [
